# Findings the "Scan image" step of tests.yml's `image` job accepts. That step already skips vulnerabilities with no
# fix yet (ignore-unfixed), so everything here HAS a fix, just not one we can apply: it ships in an upstream image
# we build FROM, or in a tool inside it. Every entry carries `exp:`: past that date the finding fails CI again, so
# it gets re-checked rather than forgotten. Prefer merging Dependabot's base-image bump (see .github/dependabot.yml)
# and deleting the entry over extending the date.

# broker and sqlite-web (python:3.14-slim): pip's bundled copies of msgpack, setuptools and urllib3 in the base
# image's own pip. pip is not on the broker's PATH at runtime (the app runs from /app/.venv, which has none) and never
# runs in either container. Goes away with the next python:3.14-slim that ships a newer pip.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 exp:2026-12-01
CVE-2025-47273 exp:2026-12-01
CVE-2026-97687 exp:2026-12-01
CVE-2026-97689 exp:2026-12-01

# broker and sqlite-web (python:3.14-slim): msgpack 1.1.2 in the same pip (memory leak deserializing maps), fixed in
# 1.2.3. Same reasoning as above: pip never runs in either container.
CVE-2026-114613 exp:2026-12-01

# caddy: golang.org/x/net/html DoS via crafted HTML input (HIGH), fixed in x/net 0.62.0. Vendored in the upstream
# binary (v0.59.0); waiting on a Caddy release that bumps it.
CVE-2026-78661 exp:2026-12-01

# broker and sqlite-web (python:3.14-slim): zlib1g 1.3.1-1+b1, fixed in Debian as 1.3.1-1+deb13u1 but not yet in the
# upstream image. The flaw is in zlib's gz* file API, which neither image reads gzip files through (Python's zlib
# module uses inflate/deflate streams). Goes away with the next python:3.14-slim rebuild.
CVE-2026-85091 exp:2026-12-01

# fluent-bit (debian 13.7): libpq5 17.11-0+deb13u1, PostgreSQL's client library, fixed in Debian as 17.12-0+deb13u1 but
# not yet in fluent/fluent-bit:5.2.0. Nearly all are flaws in the PostgreSQL server (code run by SQL functions,
# extensions, reindexdb); Fluent Bit only links the client library for its pgsql output, which fluent-bit.yaml doesn't
# use (it tails logs and sends them over HTTP and remote write), so nothing in the image talks to a PostgreSQL server.
# Goes away with the next fluent-bit rebuild.
CVE-2026-116304 exp:2026-11-29
CVE-2026-116306 exp:2026-11-29
